--
N5008 [temp.inst]/4: view_interface<ref_view<int[3]>> is instantiated as a
BASE of ref_view<int[3]>; its auto-returning members were converted eagerly
at that point, `derived().begin()` named the not-yet-complete derived class,
the conversion failed and the bodies -- including the begin_fn::operator()
instance created on the way -- were dropped for good, so `rg::begin(rv)`
returned `auto` (libstdc++ ranges: `arr | views::take(3)` had no usable
begin()).  A body whose conversion fails while a class is being elaborated is
now restored and re-queued for the end-of-unit drain (converted on demand
earlier if a call needs its return type).  Non-vacuous: the last assertion
states a wrong value and must FAIL.
